  "enhanced_information": "The patient's presentation of nonproductive cough, sharp chest pain, erythematous facial rash, history of miscarriages, and joint symptoms strongly suggests systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE). The most consistent and medically supported finding in further evaluation would likely be low serum levels of C3 and C4, indicative of the immune complex-mediated inflammation typical in SLE. This aligns with standard medical consensus and is supported by evidence linking lupus with reduced complement components.",
